CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "ab04d749-0a82-40c2-9a6c-22bcd0ab5c9a",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T22:04:48Z",
  "ticket_id": "a171-6c65",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "Part B of the epic scrutiny pipeline includes a \"residual state\" probe that forces a codebase grep when the epic involves path deprecation, relocation, or rename \u2014 verified by a test simulating a \"move files from A to B\" epic",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (the pipeline includes a probe) that will remain true after implementation, phrased as ongoing behavior despite the verification method being a one-time test"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Part C's trigger condition activates on SCs that reference moving, deprecating, removing, or renaming a file or directory \u2014 not only on SCs that reference modifying a file consumed by 2+ others",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior defining when Part C's trigger activates, independent of any one-time task completion"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The preplanning red team taxonomy includes a \"Residual References\" category and an escalate_to_epic finding type; blue-team-filter.md is updated to recognize and triage escalate_to_epic findings. When the orchestrator applies an escalate_to_epic finding, it appends a new SC to the epic description via ticket edit and emits REPLAN_ESCALATE: brainstorm \u2014 verified by asserting the epic description contains the new SC text, not that a comment exists",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behaviors (taxonomy includes category, orchestrator applies findings, epic descriptions updated) that persist after implementation, not one-time completion tasks"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Brainstorm scenario analysis findings that expose gaps in the SCs trigger SC revision. The pipeline halts and presents revised SCs to the user via AskUserQuestion for re-approval before proceeding \u2014 including in replan paths where the approval gate was previously passed. Verified by a test exercising the replan-triggered re-approval flow",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where scenario analysis triggers SC revision and re-approval gates are enforced, including in replan paths"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Behavioral test with RED baseline: first confirm unmodified pipeline does NOT trigger a residual-state finding for a \"move from A to B\" epic; then confirm modified pipeline triggers Part B probe + Part C scan + RESIDUAL_REFERENCES finding in review output",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time verification task to confirm pipeline behavior changes, with completion-flavored language about confirming and testing"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The brainstorm-preplanning replan cascade is bounded by sprint.max_replan_cycles \u2014 escalate_to_epic then REPLAN_ESCALATE then SC revision cannot exceed the configured cycle limit",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes an ongoing system constraint that remains true after implementation, where replan cascades are bounded by a configurable cycle limit"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When this epic is complete, Part B of the epic scrutiny pipeline contains a \"residual state\" probe that detects path deprecation/relocation/rename in epic specs and runs a codebase grep to count references to the deprecated path\n\u2190 Satisfies: \"Part B includes a residual state probe\"",
      "original_section": "DD",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (presence and function of a probe in Part B) that persists after completion, not the completion event itself"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When this epic is complete, Part C's trigger condition fires when SCs reference moving, deprecating, removing, or renaming a file or directory \u2014 not only when SCs reference modifying a consumed file\n\u2190 Satisfies: \"Part C trigger activates on moving/deprecating/removing/renaming\"",
      "original_section": "DD",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (Part C's trigger firing on specific conditions) that persists after the work is complete"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When this epic is complete, the preplanning red team taxonomy includes a Residual References category with an escalate_to_epic finding type, blue-team-filter.md recognizes the type, and the orchestrator appends a new SC to the epic description via ticket edit when applying escalate_to_epic findings\n\u2190 Satisfies: \"Red team has Residual References category + escalate_to_epic\"",
      "original_section": "DD",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capabilities (taxonomy includes category, filter recognizes type, orchestrator appends SC) that persist after completion rather than a one-time task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When this epic is complete, brainstorm scenario analysis findings that expose SC gaps trigger SC revision with mandatory user re-approval via AskUserQuestion before proceeding \u2014 including in replan paths\n\u2190 Satisfies: \"Scenario analysis findings trigger SC revision with re-approval\"",
      "original_section": "DD",
      "classification": {
        "label": "uncertain",
        "ranking": 2,
        "rationale": "mixes durable system behavior (scenario analysis triggers revision and re-approval) with transitional task framing (brainstorm findings, expose gaps), making it unclear whether this describes an end-state capability or a one-time completion activity"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When this epic is complete, a behavioral test with RED baseline confirms the end-to-end fix: unmodified pipeline does NOT trigger a residual-state finding; modified pipeline triggers Part B + Part C + RESIDUAL_REFERENCES finding\n\u2190 Satisfies: \"Behavioral test confirms end-to-end fix\"",
      "original_section": "DD",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes completion of a specific test validation task that confirms a fix, not an ongoing durable property of the system"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When this epic is complete, the brainstorm-preplanning replan cascade is bounded by sprint.max_replan_cycles\n\u2190 Satisfies: \"Replan cascade bounded by sprint.max_replan_cycles\"",
      "original_section": "DD",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system constraint that will remain true after completion, though the phrasing mixes outcome language with property description"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
